e="other"><bold>Agostini JV, Concato J, Inouye SK.</bold> Improving sedative-hypnotic prescribing in older hospitalized patients: provider-perceived benefits and barriers of a computer-based reminder. J Gen Intern Med. 2008 DOI <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s11606-007-0238-9">10.1007/s11606-007-0238-9</ext-link>.</citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="other"><bold>Graber ML, Mathew A.</bold> Performance of a web-based clinical diagnosis support system for internists. J Gen Intern Med. 2008 DOI <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s11606-007-0271-8">10.1007/s11606-007-0271-8</ext-link>.</citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Berg</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><source>Rationalizing Medical Work: Decision-Support Techniques and Medical Practices</source><year>1997</year><publisher-loc>Cambridge</publisher-loc><publisher-name>MIT Press</publisher-name></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Berg M. Rationalizing Medical Work: Decision-Support Techniques and Medical Practices. Cambridge: MIT Press; 1997. </citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Berg</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Patient care information systems and health care work: a sociotechnical approach</article-title><source>Int J Med Inform</source><year>1999</year><volume>55</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>87</fpage><lpage>101</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1386-5056(99)00011-8</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Berg M. Patient care information systems and health care work: a sociotechnical approach. Int J Med Inform. 1999;55(2):87&#x02013;101. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10530825</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><label>17.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aarts</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Berg</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A tale of two hospitals: a sociotechnical appraisal of the introduction of computerized physician order entry in two Dutch hospitals</article-title><source>Medinfo</source><year>2004</year><volume>11</volume><issue>Pt 2</issue><fpage>999</fpage><lpage>1002</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Aarts J, Berg M. A tale of two hospitals: a sociotechnical appraisal of the introduction of computerized physician order entry in two Dutch hospitals. Medinfo. 2004;11(Pt 2):999&#x02013;1002. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15360962</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR18"><label>18.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aarts</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Doorewaard</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Berg</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Understanding implementation: the case of a computerized physician order entry system in a large Dutch university medical center</article-title><source>J Am Med Inform Assoc</source><year>2004</year><volume>11</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>207</fpage><lpage>216</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1197/jamia.M1372</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Aarts J, Doorewaard H, Berg M. Understanding implementation: the case of a computerized physician order entry system in a large Dutch university medical center. J Am Med Inform Assoc. 2004;11(3):207&#x02013;16. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14764612</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR19"><label>19.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><source>Diffusion of Innovation</source><year>1995</year><edition>5</edition><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Free Press</publisher-name></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Rogers E. Diffusion of Innovation, 5th ed. New York: Free Press; 1995. </citation></ref><ref id="CR20"><label>20.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ware</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Hays</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Methods for measuring patient satisfaction with specific medical encounters</article-title><source>Med Care</source><year>1988</year><volume>26</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>393</fpage><lpage>402</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00005650-198804000-00008</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Ware JE Jr, Hays RD. Methods for measuring patient satisfaction with specific medical encounters. Med Care. 1988;26(4):393&#x02013;402. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3352332</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR21"><label>21.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Knottnerus</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Weel</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Muris</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of Diagnostic Procedures</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>2002</year><volume>324</volume><fpage>477</fpage><lpage>80</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmj.324.7335.477</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Knottnerus JA, van Weel C, Muris JM. Evaluation of diagnostic procedures. BMJ. 2002;324:477&#x02013;80. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11859054</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>